9]]}, {"t": " **", "lp": -0.21418224275112152, "top": [[" **", -0.21418224275112152], [" `", -1.6475270986557007]]}, {"t": "`", "lp": -0.24255873262882233, "top": [["`", -0.24255873262882233], ["ic", -1.5428193807601929]]}, {"t": "ic", "lp": -0.00027988298097625375, "top": [["ic", -0.00027988298097625375], [" ic", -9.287230491638184]]}, {"t": "x", "lp": -0.0010960145154967904, "top": [["x", -0.0010960145154967904], ["X", -8.687015533447266]]}, {"t": "`", "lp": -0.00028405647026374936, "top": [["`", -0.00028405647026374936], ["**", -9.115407943725586]]}, {"t": "**:", "lp": -0.2904089391231537, "top": [["**:", -0.2904089391231537], ["**", -1.3785855770111084]]}, {"t": " Intel", "lp": -0.003934843000024557, "top": [[" Intel", -0.003934843000024557], [" one", -6.362242698669434]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function: Step-by-Step Explanation\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line.\n\n## The Setup\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (compiler paths, library paths, etc.). The `--force` flag forces the environment to be set up even if it appears already configured. Without this, `icx`/`icpx` wouldn't be found.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nThis makes the script exit immediately if any command returns a non-zero status (an error). A safety net so a failed command doesn't cascade into confusing downstream errors.\n\n## The CMake Configuration\n\n```bash\ncmake -S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\" -B \"${srcdir}/build\" -G Ninja\n```\n- `-S`: **S**ource directory (where the source code lives)\n- `-B`: **B**uild directory (where build artifacts go)\n- `-G Ninja`: Use the **Ninja** build system (fast, minimal output) instead of Make\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\n```\nOptimize for performance (`-O3`-level optimizations, no debug symbols). This is why `!debug` is set in options.\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr -DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib\n```\n- Install prefix: `/usr` (standard system location)\n- Install lib dir: `lib` (not `lib64` \u2014 important for Arch's multiarch layout)\n\n## The Compilers\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=icx -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=icpx\n```\nUse Intel's compilers:\n- **`icx`**: Intel"}